---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Journey Through Bethlehem collects and uses information on this website."
>
  <article class="wrap page-title prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      Journey Through Bethlehem (“we,” “us,” or “our”) is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit journeythroughbethlehem.org.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when you interact with our website:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact & Inquiry Data:</strong> Name, email address, phone number, and any details submitted through email to
        <a href="mailto:team@journeythroughbethlehem.org">team@journeythroughbethlehem.org</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Event Registration & Volunteering:</strong> Information submitted to register for attendance (via Ticket Tailor), volunteer roles (via SignUpGenius), or group reservations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Donations:</strong> Payment and receipt details processed by Stripe when you give to Faith & Fellowship Foundation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email & Newsletter Signups:</strong> Email address provided to receive updates and announcements, when that option is offered.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This static website does not run analytics or advertising pixels. We do not collect device and usage data on this site for tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use collected data for legitimate operational purposes, including to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to questions, comments, and inquiries.</li>
      <li>Coordinate event details, volunteer schedules, and attendee logistics.</li>
      <li>Process donations through Stripe for Faith & Fellowship Foundation.</li>
      <li>Send site announcements, event updates, and news (with opt-out options).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      This static site does not set essential cookies of its own, and it does not use Google Analytics or Squarespace tracking. Ticket Tailor and Stripe may set cookies on their own pages when you reserve tickets or complete a donation. We do not use a cookie banner because this site does not include non-essential tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Sharing of Information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We only share information with trusted third-party service providers that assist in operating this website, hosting ticket reservations, or processing donations — including Ticket Tailor and Stripe — bound by their own privacy terms and confidentiality obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
    <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Request the correction or deletion of your personal data.</li>
      <li>Unsubscribe from email updates via the link provided in messages, or by writing to us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To opt out of Ticket Tailor or Stripe communications, use the controls those services provide or contact us and we will help.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:</p>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:team@journeythroughbethlehem.org">team@journeythroughbethlehem.org</a></p>
    <p>Last updated: August 30, 2026</p>
  </article>
</Base>
